.TH NOIRE 1 "August 2026" "Noire 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
noire \- control Noire through its GPUI interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B noire
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B noire
opens the dark GPUI control interface for the per-user Noire daemon.
Closing the window keeps the controller in the system tray by default and never
stops the daemon or removes its virtual microphone.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the installed version.
.TP
.BR \-\-minimized
Start with the window hidden in the system tray.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/noire/config.toml
Per-user configuration. The package manager does not create or remove this file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/noire/ui.toml
Desktop-only start-minimized and close-to-tray preferences.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR noirectl (1),
.BR noired (1)
